WEBVTT

00:03.169 --> 00:06.881
It sure is a beautiful day, huh, Gramps?

01:43.770 --> 01:47.565
SLICE SLICE DANCE

01:50.068 --> 01:51.694
Hey, who are you?

01:52.445 --> 01:55.031
Freeze! Show a visitor pass
or employee ID, or I'll--

02:03.581 --> 02:06.125
I'll leave the rest to you, Gaku.

02:06.126 --> 02:07.752
What? I'm doing this alone?

02:08.586 --> 02:10.754
Is there anything you wanna mention to me?

02:10.755 --> 02:13.715
They only have restrooms on odd floors,
so be careful.

02:13.716 --> 02:14.634
Aight.

02:15.468 --> 02:17.554
<i>Intruders detected.</i>

02:18.096 --> 02:21.390
<i>All combatants, collect your weapons
and head to the first floor.</i>

02:21.391 --> 02:23.183
<i>Non-combatants, to the shelters</i>

02:23.184 --> 02:24.893
<i>- located on each floor.</i>
- Intruders?

02:24.894 --> 02:26.562
No way, you serious?

02:26.563 --> 02:28.564
<i>The intruders are two individuals.</i>

02:28.565 --> 02:29.565
Two?

02:29.566 --> 02:31.316
<i>- Both are armed.</i>
- Useless guards.

02:31.317 --> 02:32.526
<i>Motives are unknown.</i>

02:32.527 --> 02:34.653
<i>They must be idiots.</i>

02:34.654 --> 02:36.948
<i>Wanna bet on which department kills them?</i>

02:37.490 --> 02:38.782
Aren't you going?

02:38.783 --> 02:41.118
I'll pass. I've got a lot of work to do.

02:41.119 --> 02:44.330
Besides, we're on the third floor.
There's no way they'll get--

02:46.332 --> 02:47.333
What the?

03:06.811 --> 03:07.854
Awesome.

03:10.064 --> 03:11.524
I gotta go to the bathroom.

03:13.234 --> 03:14.652
What floor am I on now?

03:18.656 --> 03:20.741
Fire away, guys. Shoot him up.

03:20.742 --> 03:21.951
Roger.

03:23.119 --> 03:26.663
And in three, two, one...

03:26.664 --> 03:28.333
Practice, over.

03:44.515 --> 03:45.807
Aw, shit.

03:45.808 --> 03:47.852
I shoulda skipped work today.

03:58.613 --> 04:00.615
Pull yourself together, Takebe.

04:01.282 --> 04:03.742
You gotta set an example
for the young guys.

04:03.743 --> 04:04.827
Mr. Inoda!

04:05.453 --> 04:06.620
How many dead?

04:06.621 --> 04:09.666
I'd say about 40
from the first to third floors,

04:10.250 --> 04:12.125
in the two minutes since intrusion.

04:12.126 --> 04:13.670
So, a monster.

04:20.468 --> 04:22.428
That felt good.

04:38.194 --> 04:40.112
Did you hear that noise?

04:40.113 --> 04:41.489
Yeah.

04:56.504 --> 04:58.298
It's good to see you, Boss.

04:58.881 --> 05:00.048
Did you lose some weight?

05:00.049 --> 05:02.509
Good to see you, Uda.

05:02.510 --> 05:05.554
Did you bring Gaku of all people?

05:05.555 --> 05:06.680
Yeah.

05:06.681 --> 05:09.600
That idiot's getting carried away.

05:10.143 --> 05:11.727
COLD GREEN TEA - COLD OSHIRUKO SODA

05:11.728 --> 05:15.606
I'm sorry we had to have you
act like a spy for a whole year.

05:16.524 --> 05:17.692
Where are the others?

05:18.401 --> 05:20.068
Downstairs, standing guard.

05:20.069 --> 05:24.531
The JAA pays really well
and has great employee benefits.

05:24.532 --> 05:26.909
The work environment
was way better than yours.

05:28.494 --> 05:29.495
Make any friends?

05:30.246 --> 05:32.372
I did, actually.

05:32.373 --> 05:34.666
But they work in R&D on the third floor,

05:34.667 --> 05:36.085
so they'd be dead by now.

05:37.045 --> 05:37.920
Sorry about that.

05:38.755 --> 05:39.589
No worries.

05:40.089 --> 05:43.384
So, we're initiating the plan?

05:44.052 --> 05:46.596
It's time to hit reset on the rotten JAA.

05:47.430 --> 05:50.141
I'll create a new order for this world.

06:01.444 --> 06:02.695
Stop right there!

06:03.404 --> 06:05.822
This building is now under
Mr. Slur's control.

06:05.823 --> 06:07.700
If you wanna live, get lost.

06:25.635 --> 06:26.677
Something's here...

06:49.992 --> 06:51.869
That old guy gives me goosebumps.

07:25.236 --> 07:26.070
Huh?

07:26.612 --> 07:28.030
Nope. No way.

07:34.579 --> 07:36.038
Do you think that's Gaku?

07:37.373 --> 07:40.710
What a surprise.
The Ghost of the JAA lives.

07:41.627 --> 07:43.921
I suppose we should hurry.

07:54.140 --> 07:55.599
Ouch.

07:55.600 --> 07:58.477
You said you'd weave a web when we landed!

07:58.478 --> 08:00.021
I did. For myself.

08:01.397 --> 08:02.231
It's you...

08:04.942 --> 08:07.320
Uzuki, you were alive?

08:09.864 --> 08:12.116
Long time no see, Sakamoto.

08:12.742 --> 08:17.079
It's a bit dismaying to see
that an old friend has gotten fat.

08:17.747 --> 08:19.499
<i>He knows Mr. Sakamoto?</i>

08:21.709 --> 08:23.544
Say hi to Sakamoto for me.

08:24.670 --> 08:26.881
<i>It's him... from back then!</i>

08:27.507 --> 08:29.759
Please forget that old name of mine.

08:30.468 --> 08:32.595
I prefer the name Slur.

08:33.221 --> 08:35.723
<i>Slur? It's this guy?!</i>

08:36.724 --> 08:39.644
Why did you put a bounty on me now,
after all this time?

08:40.436 --> 08:42.063
What are you after?

08:42.730 --> 08:44.732
That's a lot of questions.

08:45.733 --> 08:49.195
I don't remember you being so talkative.

08:50.947 --> 08:52.114
Mr. Sakamo--

08:55.618 --> 08:59.288
No! You can't sever my connections!

09:00.665 --> 09:01.541
What?

09:02.625 --> 09:03.876
Apart!

09:10.758 --> 09:12.634
You let him slip away?

09:12.635 --> 09:13.677
I did?

09:13.678 --> 09:15.929
Mr. Sakamoto, you're bleeding!

09:15.930 --> 09:16.889
Shin...

09:25.273 --> 09:26.524
Both of you, stay back.

09:27.024 --> 09:28.401
- Let me--
- I said stay back!

09:31.070 --> 09:32.029
This is mine.

09:33.864 --> 09:38.326
They say you never know
when it's your turn to die.

09:38.327 --> 09:39.912
Right, Sakamoto?

09:47.878 --> 09:50.172
What's wrong? Come get me.

09:51.215 --> 09:53.634
Wasting time is wasting life, you know.

09:57.930 --> 09:59.139
Mr. Sakamoto!

09:59.140 --> 10:01.683
Boss, shall I take care of it?

10:01.684 --> 10:04.645
It's okay. You must be tired
from all the work.

10:05.396 --> 10:09.525
Also, I'm kind of enjoying this.
It's like a reunion.

10:10.192 --> 10:11.944
Don't you think, Sakamoto?

10:15.489 --> 10:17.742
Would you like to try and kill me again?

10:25.374 --> 10:28.252
Looking at you now
reminds me of my young self.

10:28.919 --> 10:30.963
The naivety is aggravating to watch.

10:37.136 --> 10:38.095
<i>What just happened?</i>

10:40.973 --> 10:44.976
Those with half-baked ideals end up
bringing misfortune to those around them.

10:44.977 --> 10:47.438
"Embody clear killing intent."

10:48.022 --> 10:49.982
They taught us that at the JCC, remember?

10:50.691 --> 10:53.693
I wasn't top of the class
like you and your friends,

10:53.694 --> 10:55.988
but after graduating,
I finally understand.

10:56.572 --> 10:58.491
Killing requires no emotion.

11:04.205 --> 11:07.166
Let me show you an example.

11:10.586 --> 11:11.586
Hmm?

11:11.587 --> 11:15.091
I'm so sorry, Mr. Sakamoto! It's my fault...

11:16.550 --> 11:17.675
Young boy.

11:17.676 --> 11:20.805
You'd do better if you took your life,
rather than apologize.

11:21.430 --> 11:23.349
Isn't that right, Sakamoto?

11:24.141 --> 11:26.685
At this rate, you will die,
and so will these two.

11:27.812 --> 11:31.148
I know you've been out of the game
but you can't be that out of touch.

11:32.400 --> 11:33.776
Come on, give me your all.

11:34.693 --> 11:36.195
That's the only path left.

11:37.196 --> 11:38.906
I'm not a hit man anymore.

11:39.949 --> 11:44.370
Letting me live
means you kill someone else.

11:48.916 --> 11:52.128
I heard you have a daughter, Sakamoto.

11:56.715 --> 11:58.342
<i>This threatening aura...</i>

11:59.510 --> 12:00.636
<i>There it is.</i>

12:23.033 --> 12:24.118
Welcome back,

12:25.244 --> 12:26.662
Taro Sakamoto.

12:29.665 --> 12:31.750
Don't screw it up this time.

12:37.756 --> 12:38.841
Mr. Sakamoto!

12:43.220 --> 12:44.138
Nope. No way.

12:49.643 --> 12:51.561
Things were just getting fun.

12:51.562 --> 12:52.645
Nah, man.

12:52.646 --> 12:55.608
You didn't tell me
about that crazy old guy.

13:20.424 --> 13:21.258
Uda, would you?

13:21.884 --> 13:22.927
On it.

13:43.447 --> 13:44.281
I don't need it.

13:57.753 --> 13:58.629
Let's go, Gaku.

14:03.842 --> 14:05.426
<i>Man, what a battle.</i>

14:05.427 --> 14:08.221
C'mon, Boss, I wanna see you crush 'em.

14:08.222 --> 14:09.431
Give me a break.

14:15.229 --> 14:16.063
Not so fast.

14:16.647 --> 14:17.814
I won't let you get away.

14:17.815 --> 14:20.568
It was good seeing you, Sakamoto.

14:26.198 --> 14:27.032
Bye for now.

14:35.708 --> 14:36.542
I owe you,

14:38.085 --> 14:39.003
Uda.

14:39.587 --> 14:42.756
Oh, no. Don't mention it.

15:12.745 --> 15:15.121
Mr. Sakamoto! I'm so sorry.

15:15.122 --> 15:17.499
You took off your apron for us.

15:18.125 --> 15:19.084
I'm all right.

15:33.849 --> 15:34.808
You're...

15:35.392 --> 15:36.352
Come on, Boss,

15:37.686 --> 15:39.313
let's ditch this place.

15:44.443 --> 15:46.195
Losing an arm messes with your balance.

15:47.947 --> 15:49.615
They... left?

15:53.202 --> 15:56.622
<i>That day in September, 20XX,</i>

15:57.206 --> 16:00.125
<i>176 were killed,</i>

16:00.960 --> 16:02.336
<i>three were injured,</i>

16:02.920 --> 16:04.672
<i>and one went missing.</i>

16:05.714 --> 16:09.009
<i>It had been six months
since Slur's hits on hit men had begun,</i>

16:09.593 --> 16:12.553
<i>and the number of professional hit men
in Japan</i>

16:12.554 --> 16:15.390
<i>had been reduced to a quarter.</i>

16:15.391 --> 16:20.812
A FEW DAYS AFTER THE ATTACK ON THE JAA

16:20.813 --> 16:21.980
IKORAIZAKA HOSPITAL

16:21.981 --> 16:25.566
<i>We're here at Tokyo's new landmark,
the Leaning Tower of Tokyo,</i>

16:25.567 --> 16:27.944
<i>where many tourists are flooding the town,</i>

16:27.945 --> 16:30.739
<i>disrupting the daily lives of the locals.</i>

16:31.323 --> 16:32.699
<i>- Next up, the Bloodbath</i>
- Taro,

16:32.700 --> 16:34.325
<i>- Bake Off!</i>
- want some <i>daifuku?</i>

16:34.326 --> 16:35.244
Yes, please.

16:35.828 --> 16:38.496
Y'know, that body of yours
looks like a <i>daifuku</i>, too.

16:38.497 --> 16:41.041
Mr. Sakamoto, you're eating too much.

16:43.752 --> 16:45.169
Are you lost?

16:45.170 --> 16:49.258
<i>I can't go in. How could I possibly
show my face to him right now?</i>

16:50.300 --> 16:51.467
Young boy.

16:51.468 --> 16:54.471
You'd do better if you took your life,
rather than apologize.

16:55.139 --> 16:57.056
<i>After fighting that death row inmate,</i>

16:57.057 --> 16:59.642
<i>I thought I got a little better at combat.</i>

16:59.643 --> 17:02.479
<i>But at the JAA,
I was nothing more than a burden.</i>

17:03.063 --> 17:04.397
<i>Damn it.</i>

17:04.398 --> 17:07.901
<i>I should at least
leave this luxury fruit basket for him.</i>

17:11.030 --> 17:13.239
Why do you have to come with me?

17:13.240 --> 17:16.493
Because you'll start a fight
if you go alone, Hyo.

17:18.871 --> 17:21.498
Hey there. How are you doin', Sakamoto?

17:22.082 --> 17:22.958
What do you want?

17:23.459 --> 17:25.085
Don't be like that.

17:26.128 --> 17:28.171
Obviously, we came to visit our friend--

17:28.172 --> 17:29.756
Cut the crap.

17:29.757 --> 17:33.010
Sakamoto, we heard
you came into contact with Slur.

17:33.594 --> 17:35.220
Yes, I met him.

17:36.346 --> 17:39.767
Nagumo, it was Uzuki. He's Slur.

17:43.562 --> 17:47.649
Does that mean
you failed to kill him that time?

17:48.275 --> 17:49.776
I sure wish you were joking.

17:49.777 --> 17:52.905
Hey, don't keep me in the dark. Who is it?

17:53.489 --> 17:57.576
Uzuki is a classmate of Sakamoto and mine,
back from the JCC days.

17:58.327 --> 18:02.372
He didn't stand out, so I can't say
I remember him much as a student.

18:04.166 --> 18:08.295
But if he's a good hit man,
why haven't I heard of him?

18:09.379 --> 18:10.797
I only heard about you three,

18:10.798 --> 18:14.885
Sakamoto, Nagumo, and Akao.

18:15.636 --> 18:19.680
Most of it was bad reputation,
but nonetheless...

18:19.681 --> 18:23.518
Is that so? Well, we never heard
your name in any rumors, Hyo.

18:23.519 --> 18:26.688
I'm gonna kill you.
I'm just a late bloomer!

18:27.314 --> 18:29.316
<i>Mr. Sakamoto's JCC years?</i>

18:29.858 --> 18:30.691
Anyway,

18:30.692 --> 18:33.861
now that we know who he is,
we'll take it from here.

18:33.862 --> 18:35.364
Sorry to bother you, Sakamoto.

18:35.906 --> 18:36.949
We're leaving already?

18:38.117 --> 18:41.161
Wait. There's something
I haven't told you yet.

18:41.912 --> 18:42.746
What is it?

18:43.372 --> 18:45.457
No more free intel.

18:46.125 --> 18:47.583
Tell me what The Order knows.

18:47.584 --> 18:51.296
I'll tell you in exchange
for the information you have on Slur.

18:55.384 --> 18:57.427
Let me make one thing clear.

18:58.762 --> 19:01.098
We are not working on this together.

19:01.723 --> 19:06.645
I heard you retired from the business
and have a family now, right?

19:07.229 --> 19:10.149
So if you stick your nose in this
with a half-baked plan,

19:10.732 --> 19:13.235
what happens to your wife and daughter
when you die?

19:15.237 --> 19:18.573
You act like a lone wolf,
with that unbothered look on your face,

19:18.574 --> 19:20.659
and I've always hated it.

19:21.243 --> 19:23.579
I won't die. Don't assume I'd get killed.

19:24.121 --> 19:25.789
How about I put you in your place?

19:32.671 --> 19:35.007
My my, you're so big.

19:37.593 --> 19:41.513
You know it's just a matter of time
before you die, don't you?

19:44.600 --> 19:45.767
Even if that were true,

19:46.602 --> 19:49.021
as a father,
there are times you can't back down.

19:50.063 --> 19:53.066
I want to protect the people dear to me
with my own two hands.

19:54.693 --> 19:57.279
You can't trust anyone else, huh?

19:57.905 --> 19:59.573
I used to think that.

20:00.449 --> 20:01.283
But not anymore.

20:08.916 --> 20:12.336
<i>A magnetic force? The MRI! Damn it!</i>

20:12.961 --> 20:13.795
Hyo.

20:14.421 --> 20:18.592
Please give me any information about Slur.

20:19.176 --> 20:20.969
I want to protect my family.

20:23.222 --> 20:26.225
<i>I never would've dreamed of a day
he'd be asking for my help.</i>

20:28.810 --> 20:32.606
Due to JAA rules, I can't leak
classified information to a civilian.

20:33.482 --> 20:34.607
But if I were you,

20:34.608 --> 20:37.402
I'd probably look in the JCC Databank.

20:40.239 --> 20:41.155
Thanks.

20:41.156 --> 20:44.159
Hey! You're supposed to trade information!

20:44.701 --> 20:48.704
You're so naive, Hyo. That's why you
end up with the short end of the stick.

20:48.705 --> 20:49.623
Shut up!

20:52.251 --> 20:54.085
Sorry for all the racket.

20:54.086 --> 20:55.378
It's all good.

20:55.379 --> 20:57.255
Whoa!

20:57.256 --> 20:58.965
That's quite a statement piece.

20:58.966 --> 20:59.967
I'm gonna kill you.

21:00.968 --> 21:04.805
I didn't think The Order had someone
with a warm heart like that.

21:05.430 --> 21:07.391
He's always been kind.

21:09.893 --> 21:12.396
Oh, this! Uh, you see...

21:13.730 --> 21:16.774
It's a get-well basket,
but I failed to give it to you.

21:16.775 --> 21:17.775
Why?

21:17.776 --> 21:20.903
Because I was the one weighing you down.

21:20.904 --> 21:22.364
I was too ashamed to see you.

21:24.366 --> 21:27.911
In that moment, when Slur mentioned Hana,

21:29.162 --> 21:33.917
<i>I was so close to losing it.
Your voice brought me back to my senses.</i>

21:36.753 --> 21:38.880
You're helping me all the time.

21:40.132 --> 21:41.717
I'm counting on you.

21:42.926 --> 21:45.929
C'mon, that's a line
I want to hear for real!

21:46.555 --> 21:50.434
Anyway, we now have a lead
on how to get to Slur.

21:51.226 --> 21:54.021
Shin, let's head to the JCC next.

21:54.521 --> 21:55.355
Yes, sir!

23:23.944 --> 23:25.946
Subtitle translation by: Yuka Kristi
